<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">12032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Seventeen members of a single family were among fifty-two civilians killed in Sudan when a drone struck a convoy traveling to mourn victims of an earlier attack in West <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɔːrdəˈfɑːn">Kordofan</phoneme>.</s> <s>That same day, drones struck a hospital and a school in White Nile State, killing nine more — sixty-one people dead across multiple states in a single afternoon.</s> <s>Sudan's civil war is now waged by air across the country's full breadth, largely unseen, beneath the world's attention to the Persian Gulf.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Energy Secretary Chris Wright posted — then deleted — that the United States Navy had been quietly escorting commercial tankers through the Strait of Hormuz, while the White House denied the account.</s> <s>That deletion confirmed what traders feared: a covert naval escort was already active on day nineteen of the war, as Brent crude briefly fell forty dollars on the report before recovering.</s> <s>The United Nations Security Council separately passed a resolution demanding Iran halt its Gulf attacks, but the text made no mention of the United States-Israeli strikes that triggered the conflict.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel struck a waterfront tent camp in Beirut where seven hundred thousand people displaced by its offensive had taken shelter, killing six.</s> <s>The <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ræmˈlɛt æl ˈbaɪ.də">Ramlet al-Baida</phoneme> encampment had no replacement — there is nowhere farther to flee on Lebanon's coast — and Lebanon ordered its army to respond.</s> <s>France is circulating a ceasefire resolution at the Security Council, though its prospects depend on the same powers that have blocked every previous attempt.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Senegal's parliament voted one hundred and thirty-five to zero to double prison terms for same-sex relations to ten years, and extended criminalization to anyone who advocates, documents, or finances opposition to the crackdown.</s> <s>Lawyers, journalists, and rights workers who report on the law's enforcement now face prison themselves.</s> <s>President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="bɑˈsiː.ruː djoˈmaɪ feɪ">Bassirou Diomaye Faye</phoneme>, who came to power promising reform, must now decide whether to sign it into law.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Somalia's two largest federal states, Puntland and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdʒuː.bə.lænd">Jubaland</phoneme>, refused to recognize the country's new constitution, boycotting the ratification vote after President Hassan Sheikh <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="moʊˈhɑː.muːd">Mohamud</phoneme> broke his pledge to delay the process.</s> <s>Under Somalia's federal compact, peripheral states hold an explicit veto — and both have now invoked it.</s> <s>Puntland's leaders are weighing a formal declaration of deeper autonomy that could fracture the Somali state.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Seven hundred and seventy-eight Indian sailors are stranded aboard twenty-four ships on the western side of the Strait of Hormuz, where Iran has warned every transiting vessel is a target.</s> <s>New Delhi is monitoring all twenty-eight vessels in the Gulf but has announced no plan to extract the crews.</s> <s>These sailors are among the most direct human costs of a conflict whose architects are thousands of miles away.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's talks with the International Monetary Fund ended after fourteen days without agreement, leaving a one-point-two billion dollar disbursement from its seven billion dollar bailout at risk.</s> <s>Hormuz-driven energy costs have upended the program's baseline assumptions, and Pakistan is already operating a four-day work week with schools closed.</s> <s>Talks continue in coming days, but the next tranche depends on a deal that has so far not been reached.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China's National People's Congress set a growth target of four-point-five percent through 2030 — the lowest in three decades — as property deflation and Gulf oil costs compound.</s> <s>Beijing is publicly managing expectations for a world where the Strait of Hormuz stays disrupted and United States tariffs persist.</s> <s>Countries across Southeast Asia and Sub-Saharan Africa that depend on Chinese demand can expect falling orders and lower commodity prices.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The International Energy Agency coordinated the release of four hundred million barrels from strategic reserves across thirty-one countries — and global oil prices still rose fifteen percent.</s> <s>Traders are pricing future supply risk, not today's inventory, and no stockpile release can remove the fear of a permanently closed strait.</s> <s>Nations without strategic reserves — across South Asia and the Pacific Islands — face months of hundred-dollar crude with no cushion to absorb it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Malaysia raised its diesel price by eighty sen to three ringgit ninety-two per litre, while holding its targeted subsidy for lower-income drivers unchanged at one ringgit ninety-nine.</s> <s>The two-tier structure deliberately passes the oil shock to wealthier consumers while shielding those most exposed to fuel costs.</s> <s>A weekly price review is due on <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">18032026</say-as>, with crude markets at their most volatile in years.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Astrophysicists have solved a mystery that has stood for decades: what makes some stellar explosions outshine entire galaxies.</s> <s>A supernova detected last December revealed a magnetar at its core — a neutron star spinning thousands of times per second that hurled charged particles outward and multiplied the explosion's brightness a hundredfold.</s> <s>Published Wednesday in Nature, the findings confirm a hypothesis first proposed in 2010 and may reshape how astronomers model the most violent events in the known universe.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>United States President Donald Trump designated Anthropic, the artificial intelligence company, a supply-chain security threat after the firm refused to allow the Pentagon to use its model for autonomous lethal warfare.</s> <s>Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth gave the military six months to exit Anthropic's contracts, with no alternative supplier announced.</s> <s>Anthropic's refusal is the first publicly documented case of an American artificial intelligence company declining a direct government request to arm its technology.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Iran-linked hacking group <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hænˈdɑː.lə">Handala</phoneme> claimed to have extracted fifty terabytes of data from Stryker, a major American medical device company, citing a United States-Israeli airstrike on a school in southern Iran that killed more than a hundred and fifty people.</s> <s>Stryker said it contained the breach, but the full scope of exposed patient records remains unknown.</s> <s>Targeting a medical device company marks the first expansion of this conflict's cyberwar from military and energy targets into civilian healthcare infrastructure.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>